{
  "case_id": "2021-20-827",
  "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the aftermath of the September 11, 2001, terrorist attacks, the Central Intelligence Agency believed that Abu Zubaydah was a senior al Qaeda lieutenant likely to possess knowledge of future attacks against the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government intervened and asserted the state secrets privilege in opposition to Zubaydah's discovery request."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States Government",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government claimed that disclosure of the information Zubaydah sought would violate the state secrets privilege."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States Government",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Director said that Mitchell and Jessen's response to Zubaydah's subpoenas would, in this case, confrm or deny whether Poland had cooperated with the CIA. Id., at 129a\u2013130a. And that confrmation, the Director explained, would signifcantly harm our national secu- rity interests. Id., at 131a."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For these reasons, we conclude that in this case the state secrets privilege applies to the existence (or nonexistence) of a CIA facility in Poland. It therefore precludes further discovery into all three categories of information the Ninth Circuit concluded to be nonprivileged because, as we have explained, such discovery will inevitably confrm or deny the existence of such a facility. See supra, at 205\u2013207."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Abu Zubaydah is a terrorist. Before his detention, he was an al Qaeda-associated senior operative engaged in active hostilities against the United States. See generally Factual Return for Abu Zubaydah (ISN 10016), in Husayn v. Gates, No. 08\u2013cv\u20131360 (DDC), ECF Doc. 474\u20131, pp. 24\u201367 (Factual Return). Between 1994 and 2000, Zubaydah was the \u201ckey facilitator\u201d for the \u201cKhaldan camp,\u201d a terrorist training center in eastern Afghanistan. Id., at 37, \u00b633; see also Barhoumi v. Obama, 609 F. 3d 416, 425 (CADC 2010); National Commission on Terrorist Attacks upon the United States, The 9/11 Commission Report, pp. 59, 175 (2004) (9/11 Report)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Government \u201chas provided a reasonable explanation\u201d why Zubaydah's proposed discovery \u201ccould signifcantly harm national security interests.\u201d Ante, at 207."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0003-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Court begins at Reynolds' second step and concludes that the Government \u201chas provided a reasonable explanation\u201d why Zubaydah's proposed discovery \u201ccould significantly harm national security interests.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0003-0001",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would hold that Abu Zubaydah has demonstrated only \u201ca dubious showing of necessity\u201d for the discovery he seeks in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0004-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They waterboarded Zubaydah at least 80 times, simulated live burials in coffns for hundreds of hours, and performed rectal exams designed to establish \u201ctotal control over the detainee.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0004-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Zubaydah's lawyers tell us, the details of Zubaydah's treatment during this singular period are not yet publicly documented."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0004-0006",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And they stressed that \u201c[v]aluable discovery may proceed without requiring [Mitchell and Jessen] to confrm either the location of any particular site, or the cooperation of any particular government.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0004-0010",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 28 U. S. C. \u00a7 1782, Congress has expressly authorized federal courts to order discovery from domestic persons in aid of foreign proceedings like the ongoing Polish prosecution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0005-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "man's evidence from a judicial proceeding thanks to the pow- ers it enjoys under Article II, that claim must be carefully assessed against the competing powers Articles I and III have vested in Congress and the Judiciary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0005-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "must at least \u201cstate the particular reasons\u201d for his action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0005-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Almost 150 years after Burr, the Court reaffrmed this same understanding in United States v. Reynolds, 345 U. S. 1 (1953)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0005-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ever, contained information executive offcials knew to be false at the time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0005-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "24 (documenting alleged improper governmental withholding of information in FOIA cases); W. Weaver & R. Pallitto, State Secrets and Executive Power, 120 Pol. Sci. Q. 85, 101, 107\u2013112 (2005) (Weaver & Pallitto)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0005-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "a claim of privilege and extending instead \u201cutmost defer- ence\u201d to the Executive's mere assertion of one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0005-0006",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Reynolds drew seeks to accommodate the separation of pow- ers: It ensures that a congressional mandate to entertain a case or controversy will not be automatically frustrated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0005-0007",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Here again, I see a balance consistent with the Constitu- tion's design."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0005-0008",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "proving its case using facts obtainable through other means."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0005-0009",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "have used protective orders and other security procedures to allow sensitive governmental information to be shared\u2014"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0006-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "does the government seek to discharge that burden in this case? Zubaydah seeks evidence from Mitchell and Jessen."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0006-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The best the majority can say is this: The location of a CIA detention site in Poland qualifes as a \u201cstate secret\u201d because \u201cwe have found nothing in the eviden- tiary record that casts doubt\u201d on the declaration's conclusory assertion that national security harms could follow from ac- knowledging its existence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0006-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Looking past these problems only serves to expose an- other and maybe more fundamental one. Assume now with the government that confrming the existence of a detention site in Poland really does qualify as a state secret."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0006-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "their testimony about Zubaydah's treatment, Mitchell and Jessen might inadvertently disclose the location of their ac- tivities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0006-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Indeed, according to an amicus, the government even fled a motion in the military commission proceedings endorsing the practice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0006-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This submission faces its own problems. A litigant's ne- cessity for the evidence he seeks may inform how far a court must go in testing the government's claim of privilege."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0006-0006",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Rather than face these problems, the plurality attempts a way around them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0006-0007",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ultimately, the plurality is forced to give ground."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cb893711d795c32b66fad93265411e704163d6bf44e5c190951cfb8f3bf05e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cb893711d7-0006-0008",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the end, only one argument for dismissing this case at its outset begins to make sense."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
